        "First — pose-and-select over a superstructure. Do not solve a fixed problem: enumerate the configuration space and select which blocks, routes, data, and agents to activate, under a budget. The same act recurs at four scales — design time, run time (the epistemic gearbox), the data plane (budgeted retrieval), and the agent fabric.",
        "Second — the monotone consequence law. As warrant for a benign reading falls, the admissible set may only ever contract: the S0→S4 architecture of refusal, safe-side rounding, and the rule that the gearbox ranks the admissible set but never enlarges it. Selection is free; consequence is bounded.",
